      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits on Virginia State Route 3, about 6.7 miles east of Saluda, the county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/topping_virginia",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hummel Field, an airfield founded by early aviator Fred Hummel in 1925, sits in Topping and was donated to the county in 1970.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topping%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Topping’s wetlands and tidal marshes along the Rappahannock and Piankatank Rivers support oyster reefs and migratory waterfowl, forming part of the Chesapeake Bay ecosystem.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/topping_virginia",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The area was originally inhabited by the Nimcock tribe of the Powhatan Confederacy before European settlement displaced them upriver.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
